@kannon92 Thank you for pointing me.
As @mimowo mentioned above, I believe that this is expected behavior.
As we discussed in https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/123775, we had problems with capacities and quota management. The in-flight conditions (SuccessCriteriaMet / FailureTarget) allows them to report the fact that terminating Pods are still grabbing computing resources. After computing resources are completely freed (Pods finished), the Job can retrieve the completion conditions (`Complete` / `Failed`)

@ali-a-a Thank you for the great insight.

