Could you point the place where they mention the specifications? As I checked the documentation and API comments, I could not find the non-zero specifications to Job, while Parallel Job has non-zero completions specifications: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/job/#parallel-jobs

@mimowo my setup uses fluxcd with [`dependsOn` and `wait`](https://fluxcd.io/flux/components/kustomize/kustomizations/#wait) for a Kustomization object. This means the Kustomization waits till all resources managed by it are in ready state to signal the Kustomization is ready. The setup broke when the cluster was upgraded from 1.31 to 1.32. The job was "stuck" in the Running state and so flux wasn't proceeding further to the next Kustomization.

Since I didn't see any mention of this breaking change I submitted the issue since kubernetes has a strict policy on deprecations as far as I know. Maybe others have the same problem.

In any case I'm changing my setup a bit so it doesn't rely on the job's status.

